"helpText" = "## How to use\n1. Copy styled text.\n2. Press **⇧⌘V** where you want to paste it. It is pasted without formatting.\n- If the front app has a menu item such as Paste and Match Style or Paste without Formatting, that item is used.\n- Otherwise only the text is put back on the clipboard and ⌘V is sent. The clipboard is restored after about one second.\n- Which way was used is shown under “Last result” in the main window and at the top of the menu bar menu.\n\n## Main window\n- Shows the hotkey state and the last result, with a warning when Accessibility is not allowed or the hotkey cannot be registered.\n- “Remove Formatting from Clipboard”: leaves only the text on the clipboard. This cannot be undone.\n\n## Settings\n- Startup & Background: Open at Login (off by default), Hide main window at startup, keep running after closing the window, menu bar icon, Accessibility status, Restart and Quit buttons.\n- Hotkey: turn ⇧⌘V on or off, Change… records a key with ⌘ or ⌃ (Esc cancels), Reset to Default.\n- Paste: the menu titles to use (one per line, can be restored), whether to use them, and whether to restore the clipboard after pasting (on by default).\n- Excluded Apps: apps where ⇧⌘V is left alone. Defaults: Illustrator, Path Finder, Keynote.\n- ⌘, opens Settings and ⌘W closes it.\n\n## Hotkey\n- **⇧⌘V**: paste without formatting.\n- While an excluded app is in front, the key is not registered and does what that app assigns.\n- To stop it for a while, choose “Pause (until relaunch)” in the menu bar menu.\n\n## Permissions\n- **Accessibility**: needed to choose the front app's menu item and to send Paste (⌘V). Turn on PasteMatchStyle in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility.\n\n## Running and quitting\n- PasteMatchStyle stays in the menu bar. The hotkey works with the window closed.\n- The menu bar icon, the Dock icon, opening the app again from the Finder, or ⌘0 shows the main window.\n- Quit with “Quit PasteMatchStyle” in the menu bar menu, or ⌘Q while the app is in front.\n\n## Limitations\n- Nothing happens when the clipboard has no text (only an image, for example). Use ⌘V.\n- When a menu item is used, how much formatting is matched depends on the app.\n- Add apps that use ⇧⌘V for something else (such as the preview in VS Code) to the excluded apps.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- **Nothing happens**: check the Accessibility permission, that the hotkey is enabled, and that the front app is not excluded.\n- **Formatting remains**: the app's menu item keeps some formatting. Remove that title from the list under Paste, and the text alone is pasted.\n- **The clipboard is not restored**: check “Restore the clipboard after pasting”. Anything you copied in the meantime takes priority.\n\n## Sharing settings\n- In Settings › Sharing, Export & Import saves the settings to a file (PasteMatchStyle-Settings.plist) or reads them back, for moving to another Mac or keeping a backup. Importing asks before replacing.\n- Settings Sync keeps the settings in a folder such as iCloud Drive or Dropbox; Macs that choose the same folder share the settings, and the most recent save wins.\n- Shared: the hotkey and the paste options, including the menu item names. Launch at login, staying open, the menu bar icon and excluded apps stay on each Mac.\n\n## Privacy\n- Everything is processed on this Mac and nothing is sent out (except update checks).\n- Clipboard contents are never saved to files or logs.";
